<p>Leaning downvote &#8212; but a good start!</p>
<p>Rationale:</p>
<ul>
<li>First; I like the idea! A memetic hazard that is too harmful to the hosts for it to spread too quickly, as it's both self-destructive and kills the hosts in short order. If this were the point of the SCP, I'd have upvoted. It's nice that there's SCPs being written that /are/ manageable; a lot of more recent SCPs seem to have the Foundation constantly one step away from destruction.</li>
<li>Secondly; there were some minor spelling/grammar issues that broke the SCP tone for me; a look over by a kind editor would fix this.</li>
<li>Thirdly; the reveal of the person being real seemed unrelated to the story so far (except by name) so lessening the tension. Is this person a victim? A saboteur? A result of the virus? Any of these could work, but at the moment I can't tell which it's meant to be.</li>
</ul>

